(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the experimental setup, procedures, and safety precautions of the Electrical Machines Laboratory at LPU.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Electrical Machines Laboratory at LPU:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Laboratory Infrastructure & Machine Benches:) Tj
T*
(   The laboratory houses coupled motor-generator sets mounted on heavy vibration-dampened) Tj
T*
(   cast-iron bedplates:) Tj
T*
(   - DC Machines: Separately excited, shunt, series, and compound DC machines rated 3 kW to 5 kW.) Tj
T*
(   - AC Machines: 3-phase squirrel cage and slip-ring induction motors, salient-pole and) Tj
T*
(   cylindrical-rotor synchronous alternators.) Tj
T*
(   - Transformers: Single-phase and 3-phase two-winding transformers, autotransformers, and) Tj
T*
(   Scott-connected three-phase to two-phase transformer banks.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Experimental Procedures:) Tj
T*
(   - Load characteristics of DC shunt/compound generators.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed control of DC shunt motors below base speed \(armature resistance control\) and above) Tj
T*
(   base speed \(field flux weakening\).) Tj
T*
(   - Open-Circuit \(OCC\) and Short-Circuit \(SCC\) tests of synchronous alternators to evaluate) Tj
T*
(   synchronous impedance \($Z_s$\) and voltage regulation via the EMF and MMF methods.) Tj
T*
(   - Circle Diagram and equivalent circuit parameter extraction of 3-phase induction motors from) Tj
T*
(   No-Load and Blocked-Rotor tests.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Laboratory Safety Precautions:) Tj
T*
(   - All rotating machine couplings are enclosed in rigid metal mesh guards.) Tj
T*
(   - DC shunt motors must always be started using a 3-point or 4-point starter with field rheostat) Tj
T*
(   set to minimum resistance \(maximum flux\) to prevent catastrophic overspeed runaway.) Tj
T*
(   - Workbenches are equipped with emergency pushbuttons and 30 mA residual current circuit) Tj
T*
(   breakers \(RCCB\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the apparatus, testing methodology, and safety interlocks of the High-Voltage and Power Systems Laboratory.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   High-Voltage & Power Systems Laboratory:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. High-Voltage Apparatus:) Tj
T*
(   - High-Voltage AC Test Transformer: Single-unit or cascaded testing transformers generating up) Tj
T*
(   to 100 kV RMS at power frequency.) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-Stage Marx Impulse Generator: Generates standard $1.2/50\\,\\mu\\text{s}$ lightning) Tj
T*
(   impulse voltages up to 200-300 kV peak.) Tj
T*
(   - Sphere-Gap Voltmeter: Calibrated copper/brass spheres used for peak voltage breakdown) Tj
T*
(   calibration.) Tj
T*
(   - Oil Dielectric Test Set \(BDV Tester\): Tests mineral oil breakdown voltage according to IS) Tj
T*
(   6792.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Safety Interlocks & Protocols:) Tj
T*
(   - The high-voltage test bay is surrounded by an earthed metal mesh cage with electrical) Tj
T*
(   interlock switches on access doors; opening the gate instantly trips the high-voltage primary) Tj
T*
(   supply.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
