(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss electrical safety regulations: NFPA 70E, Lockout/Tagout \(LOTO\), and the Indian Electricity Rules \(CEA Regulations 2010\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Electrical Safety Standards & Statutory Framework:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. NFPA 70E \(Standard for Electrical Safety in the Workplace\):) Tj
T*
(   Focuses on electrical workplace safety, mandating an Electrically Safe Work Condition \(ESWC\)) Tj
T*
(   before performing maintenance. It standardizes Arc Flash Risk Assessment, calculating flash) Tj
T*
(   boundaries and specifying Arc-Rated Personal Protective Equipment \(PPE Categories 1 to 4\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Lockout / Tagout \(LOTO\) Procedures:) Tj
T*
(   Mandatory procedure requiring that energy isolating devices \(disconnect switches, circuit) Tj
T*
(   breakers\) be locked with a standardized padlock and tagged with danger warning labels. The) Tj
T*
(   worker holds the sole key, preventing accidental re-energization by others during maintenance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. CEA \(Measures Relating to Safety and Electric Supply\) Regulations 2010:) Tj
T*
(   Statutory Indian safety rules governing installation clearances, grounding resistance) Tj
T*
