(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working and synchronization procedures of an alternator using the Dark Lamp Method.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Alternator Synchronization via Three Dark Lamp Method:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Setup: Three incandescent lamps are connected across corresponding phases of the incoming) Tj
T*
(   alternator and live busbar switch \($R-R', Y-Y', B-B'$\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Visual Indication: The lamps flicker simultaneously as the frequency difference varies. When) Tj
T*
(   the frequencies are close, the lamps flicker slowly. When the phase angle difference approaches) Tj
T*
(   zero, the voltage across each lamp drops to zero, and all three lamps become DARK) Tj
T*
(   simultaneously. The synchronizing circuit breaker is closed at the exact midpoint of the dark) Tj
T*
(   period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
