(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the construction and working of a synchro error detector pair in position control systems.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Synchro Error Detector:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Synchro Transmitter \(TX\): Single-phase rotor excited with reference AC voltage $V_r) Tj
T*
(   \\sin\(\\omega t\)$. Induces 3-phase voltages in stator windings proportional to rotor position) Tj
T*
(   $\\theta_1$.) Tj
T*
(   2. Synchro Control Transformer \(CT\): Stator connected to TX stator. Induces an AC voltage in) Tj
T*
(   its rotor proportional to the sine of the angular misalignment error: $v_e\(t\) = K \\sin\(\\theta_1) Tj
T*
(   - \\theta_2\) \\sin\(\\omega t\)$. For small angles, error voltage is directly proportional to) Tj
T*
(   angular error $\(\\theta_1 - \\theta_2\)$, serving as the primary feedback sensor in servo systems.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
