(   Brake Drum Dynamometer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Construction: A cast-iron drum mounted on the motor shaft, enveloped by a friction belt) Tj
T*
(   attached to two spring balances \($S_1$ and $S_2$\). The drum has internal cooling water) Tj
T*
(   channels.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mechanical Torque Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   $$T = \(S_1 - S_2\) \\cdot g \\cdot R_{eff} \\quad [\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}]$$) Tj
T*
(   where $R_{eff}$ is effective radius \(drum radius + half belt thickness\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Shaft Power: $P_{out} = \\omega T = \\frac{2 \\pi N}{60} T \\text{ [Watts]}$. Measuring) Tj
T*
(   electrical input power yields motor efficiency: $\\eta = P_{out} / P_{in}$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
