(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the principles of Scott Connection \(T-Connection\) of transformers for 3-phase to 2-phase conversion.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Scott Connection \(T-Connection\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Main Transformer: Center-tapped primary connected across phases B and C \(ratio $1:1$\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Teaser Transformer: Primary connected between phase A and the center tap of the main) Tj
T*
(   transformer, having $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\approx 86.6\\%$ of the turns of the main transformer.) Tj
T*
(   Result: Produces two balanced secondary voltages of identical magnitude mutually displaced by) Tj
T*
(   exactly $90^\\circ$ electrical, used in electric arc furnaces and electric railway traction.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
