(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the construction and operation of an Earth Leakage Circuit Breaker \(ELCB\) vs. Residual Current Device \(RCD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   ELCB vs. RCD Operation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Voltage ELCB \(Legacy\): Connects between equipment chassis and a separate earth rod. Operates) Tj
T*
(   only if fault voltage exceeds 50V. Obsolete because broken earth wire prevents operation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Current RCD / RCCB \(Modern Standard\): Uses a Core Balance Current Transformer \(CBCT\)) Tj
T*
(   surrounding phase and neutral wires. In healthy circuits, magnetic flux cancels \($I_L - I_N =) Tj
T*
(   0$\). If current leaks to earth \($> 30\\text{ mA}$\), net flux induces secondary voltage in CBCT) Tj
T*
(   trip coil, tripping mechanism in 20-40 ms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
