(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the ethical guidelines for peer review and conflict-of-interest avoidance in scientific engineering publications.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Scholarly Peer Review Ethics:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Confidentiality: Reviewers must treat submitted manuscripts as privileged confidential) Tj
T*
(   documents, never sharing or appropriating ideas before publication.) Tj
T*
(   2. Conflict of Interest: Reviewers must decline reviewing manuscripts written by recent) Tj
T*
(   collaborators, institutional colleagues, or commercial competitors.) Tj
T*
(   3. Constructive Objectivity: Critiques must be substantiated with scientific evidence, free) Tj
T*
(   from personal hostility, and focused on improving scientific validity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
