(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the function and calibration of a Kelvin Double Bridge for precision low resistance measurement.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Kelvin Double Bridge for Low Resistance Measurement:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. The Low-Resistance Problem: Measuring resistances $< 1\\,\\Omega$ \(e.g. transformer windings,) Tj
T*
(   motor armatures\) with a Wheatstone bridge suffers severe errors from lead and contact) Tj
T*
(   resistances.) Tj
T*
(   2. Kelvin Double Bridge Innovation: Incorporates two sets of ratio arms \($P/Q$ and $p/q$\). When) Tj
T*
(   the ratio condition is balanced \($P/Q = p/q$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$R = S \\frac{P}{Q}$$) Tj
T*
(   The connecting lead resistance between unknown resistor $R$ and standard resistor $S$ is) Tj
T*
(   completely eliminated from the measurement equation, enabling micro-ohm \($10^{-6}\\,\\Omega$\)) Tj
T*
(   precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
